347	
348	## Authentication
349	
350	### Getting QuickBooks API Credentials
351	
352	1. Go to the [Intuit Developer Portal](https://developer.intuit.com/)
353	2. Create a new app or select an existing one
354	3. Get the **Client ID** and **Client Secret** from the app's keys section
355	4. Add `http://localhost:8000/callback` to the app's Redirect URIs
356	
357	### Option 1: Using Environment Variables (Recommended)
358	
359	If you have existing tokens:
360	
361	```env
362	QUICKBOOKS_CLIENT_ID=your_client_id
363	QUICKBOOKS_CLIENT_SECRET=your_client_secret
364	QUICKBOOKS_REFRESH_TOKEN=your_refresh_token
365	QUICKBOOKS_REALM_ID=your_realm_id
366	QUICKBOOKS_ENVIRONMENT=sandbox
367	```
368	
369	### Option 2: OAuth Flow
370	
371	If you don't have tokens, the server can initiate an OAuth flow that:
372	- Starts a temporary local server
373	- Opens your browser for authentication
374	- Saves tokens to your `.env` file
375	- Closes automatically when complete
